l-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":74868.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":2213.0,"requests":4}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the SDK-exposed attribute the DC session guard reads to confirm pycontribs/jira honored max_retries=0 (mirroring ADR 0087's client.max_retries read-back), so the guard fails loud rather than vacuously.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2722,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 5: 'Build a dedicated DC executor client with jira.JIRA(..., max_retries=0) plus a session guard.'","Web: DeepWiki pycontribs/jira JIRA-client docs list 'max_retries int Maximum number of retry attempts for failed requests' — constructor param confirmed, read-back attribute not documented","ADR 0087 precedent (docs/adr/0087-transport-retry.md:30): 'construction-time guard that fails fast if max_retries != 0' reads the SDK-exposed attribute; the DC analogue's read surface is unnamed","Prior plan-review cache (.rebar/cache/.../752f4e6d...json) raised the same silent-no-op risk"],"finding":"The DC executor's max_retries=0 + 'session guard' capability assertion cites the constructor param but does not name the effective SDK-exposed attribute the guard reads back to confirm pycontribs/jira honored max_retries=0. Web docs (DeepWiki pycontribs/jira) confirm the constructor ACCEPTS a max_retries int, but not the read-back surface; ADR 0087's analogous Anthropic guard reads client.max_retries, and the DC guard's equivalent is unstated.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5154e5fe9e4a7878","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 5 / Scope (DC executor client) / AC 'The dedicated DC executor client uses guarded max_retries=0'","norm_id":"n5c59c4dc4f6c96dc","priority":0.4278,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["pycontribs/jira stores the retry count on a resilient-session attribute the guard does not inspect, so the guard passes vacuously while the SDK keeps retrying underneath the single-budget executor — the exact write-multiplication the story exists to prevent"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["5 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a T3 (DC) acceptance criterion requiring exactly one bounded completion log (same fields, 512-cp message, 1,024-cp whole-log bound) for every DC terminal/exhausted outcome or cleanup failure.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5719,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent AC: 'Every terminal/exhausted outcome or cleanup failure emits exactly one completion log containing only logical id, disposition, invocation/request counts, cleanup status, retry_not_before, and one redacted message capped at 512 Unicode code points; the whole log is at most 1,024 Unicode code points.'","T2 AC mirrors this for Cloud: 'Every terminal/exhausted outcome or cleanup failure emits exactly one completion log ...'","T3 acceptance criteria list contains no completion-log emission or 1,024-code-point-bound item; its final AC is 'Failed or inconclusive observation returns non-replaying commit_unknown.'","Roster block for T3 is fully parseable, so this is a genuine absence, not indeterminate.","container pairing: parent + 72d0-0f09-1694-4010/7bc2-5203-d5f4-4a4a/a8cd-01cd-c370-454f/c6f3-cda5-c460-4c5c"],"finding":"The parent's completion-log acceptance criterion is provider-neutral ('Every terminal/exhausted outcome or cleanup failure emits exactly one completion log ...') and therefore covers DC selected outcomes, but only the Cloud child (T2) carries a completion-log emission acceptance criterion. The DC child (T3) has no acceptance criterion for emitting the single bounded completion log for its terminal/exhausted outcomes, and T1 defines only the outcome/budget contract (not log emission), while T4 covers handler result mapping (not the completion log). DC terminal/exhausted outcomes are thus partially uncovered for one-log cardinality and the 1,024-code-point serialized bound.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"faef1456ef3c451c8","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"child c6f3-cda5-c460-4c5c (RP-03 S1 T3)","norm_id":"n714b9246ab4c39b5","priority":0.3781,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A DC summary write times out (commit_unknown / exhausted_transient) and either emits zero completion logs, multiple logs, or an over-1,024-code-point log with no test pinning the cardinality/bound for the DC route."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add to child c6f3-cda5-c460-4c5c an acceptance criterion identical in structure to T2's completion-log AC, scoped to the DC executor route.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"insufficient","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the pinned jira version the max_retries=0 kwarg was verified against, and specify that the DC executor session guard reads the SDK's effective retry count (fail-loud) rather than merely passing the kwarg.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5425,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Approach 5: 'Build a dedicated DC executor client with jira.JIRA(..., max_retries=0) plus a session guard.'","transport.py:194 constructs jira.JIRA(server=..., token_auth=..., options=...) with NO max_retries kwarg today — this is a new constructor surface","_issues.py:245 comment: 'verified against jira 3.10.5' — pins the version but the plan does not restate it for the max_retries assertion","Existing precedent anthropic_model.py:139 guards 'AsyncAnthropic.max_retries must be 0' by reading the client attribute after construction","EVIDENCE CLASS: Partially-verified — jira.JIRA vendor is already used, but the max_retries=0 kwarg surface could not be observed from the library source (.venv outside snapshot)"],"finding":"The plan asserts a NEW external constructor surface, jira.JIRA(..., max_retries=0), which is not passed by the current production client construction (transport.py:194 passes only server/token_auth/options). The kwarg is a real pycontribs/jira 3.x parameter, but the plan does not name the pinned jira version it verified against, and the 'session guard' is described without stating that it reads the SDK's effective retry count (analogous to the Anthropic guard at anthropic_model.py:139). A silent rename/removal of the kwarg across a jira upgrade would otherwise leave the SDK on its default retry layer.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f15ed9ca3820d407f","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 5 / Scope (DC transport.py, retry.py); AC 'The dedicated DC executor client uses guarded max_retries=0'","norm_id":"n281a13cae2732b41","priority":0.3575,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future jira SDK upgrade renames or drops max_retries, silently reinstating the SDK's own retry layer on the DC executor route","The guard checks only that the kwarg was passed, not that the SDK's effective retry count is 0"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In Approach step 5 / the DC executor AC, state the verified jira version (e.g. 3.10.5) and require the session guard to assert the constructed client's effe